# Phase E (#47, flip brick B3) — the stage-0 SEED anchor.
#
# Most of krapped/ is machine-generated and ignored, BUT the deterministic TEXT output of
# a one-time libclang generation is COMMITTED as the bootstrap seed: post-B5 (libclang
# reducer deleted from in-tree krapper_gen) this module can no longer (re)generate its std
# container bindings, so it builds from this committed seed under
# -Pkpp.frontend.slice=seed (now its default — see root gradle.properties).
#
# Committed (deterministic, portable): the Kotlin bindings (src/), the C++ wrapper
# (slice.cc / slice.h), the forcing headers (KrapperForce_*.h — std-only #includes, no
# absolute path) and the discovered-instantiation manifest (requested.txt). Everything else
# — the compiled wrapper object (libslice.a), the cinterop .def (carries this checkout's
# absolute krapped path), generated.txt, fixups.json, *.log — stays machine-generated/
# ignored and is regenerated at build (the .def + .a by runSeedSync, a plain C++ compile).
/krapped/*
!/krapped/requested.txt
!/krapped/src
!/krapped/src/**
!/krapped/*.cc
!/krapped/*.h
